WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone is about to start!

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.320
Wait!

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.330
Soccer...

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.180
Soccer isn't meant to be used like this!

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.830
Endou-san...

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.770
C'mon, give me your best shot!

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.000
You don't even know your own abilities.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.800
So what?

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.800
I won't know unless I try!

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.460
What you're doing here isn't soccer.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.950
The ball isn't meant to hurt people!

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.970
That's right! You're making soccer feel sad!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:42.230
Hey, that's a nice way to put it!

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.550
Uh... you called yourself Tenma, right?

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.040
Yes!

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:46.470
Alpha!

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.440
Even the ball is crying from the way you use it!

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.660
Soccer must be destroyed.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.510
Therefore, through soccer, Endou Mamoru will destroy himself.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.870
As of now, we will enter the modification process for Endou Mamoru's Interruption point.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.340
It's a one on one between Alpha and Endou!

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.680
How will this game end?!

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.990
I'll stop it no matter what!

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.180
I won't let you destroy soccer!

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.020
God Hand!

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.700
G-God Hand?!

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.900
Here? Now?!

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.480
Wow!

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.600
The mutual resonance of parallel worlds!

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.260
I-I blocked it?

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.900
I did it!

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.300
I finally completed that technique!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.760
It's the mutual resonance between time and space.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:33.710
The multiple identities of Endou Mamoru throughout the parallel worlds have intervened with each other and raised their power.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.430
Proceed with caution.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:40.250
This Endou Mamoru does not exist in any of our current data.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:41.950
Yes.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:45.320
All right! Now the flow's come to our side!

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:49.630
Fei and the Dupli! We'll spread out and go for the counter!

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:50.670
Let's go!

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.670
The ball has gone to Protocol Omega!

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.350
I'll stop you!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.420
That boy is fast!

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.880
He's improving rapidly!

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.130
He's fast, so fast! What incredible speed!

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.100
Wonder...

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.040
What?!

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.270
Trap!

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:16.940
Good job, Tenma!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.190
Is that acceleration of his a result of space-time?

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:20.910
Crush him.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:25.620
Aggressive Beat!

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:31.870
He's pretty awesome!

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.490
Fei!

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.360
Zanou, watch him for the attack.

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:37.230
Yes.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:38.740
Tenma, go!

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.510
True Mach Wind!

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:46.700
Keeper Command 03!

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.070
<Boom Shout>

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.850
Goal!

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.170
All right!

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:54.810
You had amazing speed, Tenma!

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.160
Thanks!

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.460
I never thought I could go this fast myself!

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.320
They're so amazing!

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:10.010
The match resumes with Tenmas in a 1-0 lead!

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.700
Protocol Omega charges in!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:13.530
Here they come!

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.130
Shoot Command 01!

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.880
<Spinning Trans-am>

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.560
I'll stop this one too.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.020
What?

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.250
I can feel power surging through me.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.250
The intensity of that light...

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.960
Demon God Great!

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.180
Endou-san became an Avatar user?!

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.400
Wow!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.510
This is too awesome!!!

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:53.830
Great The Hand!

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:56.650
What?

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.200
H-He stopped that transcendental shoot!

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.210
Goalkeeper Endou makes a magnificent catch!

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:05.960
Tenmas this time are pretty cool!

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:09.630
What was that?

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.390
It was an Avatar!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.070
Avatar?

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:14.590
This is the effect of space-time...

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.830
To have evolved this far in so short a time span...

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.930
Why did you turn pink?

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.750
This is Exciting Gauge!

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.350
When I get excited, I turn into this!

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:27.930
See!

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.300
I will never hate soccer!

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.720
We need Coach Endou to make the soccer club.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.950
That's the main reason why we can't afford to lose here.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:40.290
Raimon's soccer club is the future of soccer.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:43.840
With a 1-0 score, Tenmas is still in the lead!

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:44.500
Fei!

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.410
Fei, are you okay?

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:49.080
Yeah.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.730
He's got enough on his plate as it is, controlling the Dupli...

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:54.620
Hey!

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.140
Mind if I join this match?

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.140
Tsurugi?

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.370
Chairman, who is that?

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:10.700
That man has the element of creating the flow of soccer.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.910
What do you mean, "element"?

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.670
His very existence creates a new direction.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:18.560
I will send you his data.

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:22.440
Yes, I have determined who he is.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:26.090
An error born out of our modification of Tsurugi Kyousuke's Interruption point.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.330
Errors can be fixed.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.450
Tsurugi!

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.130
You came!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.560
Huh? Tsurugi?

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.730
I'm not Kyousuke who you're familiar with.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:47.260
I'm Kyousuke's brother, Tsurugi Yuuichi.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.460
Yuuichi-san?

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:52.870
You're Tenma-kun, right?

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:55.360
Your legs... they're okay now?

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:57.500
I'll explain later.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.220
Right now, we need to fight them.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:07:59.930
Okay!

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:01.950
Who's that?

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:05.740
It looks like we've gained a strong ally from a parallel world.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.830
You will be correctly modified this time.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.830
We'll see about that.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.830
Switch players! Kimoro!

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.640
Tenmas switches out Kimoro for Tsurugi Yuuichi!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.550
I'm so happy that I get to play soccer with you!

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:28.930
Same here.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.710
Also, how amazing is it to be able to play with him?

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:35.340
Leave the goal to me!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.310
Now, we resume!

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.490
He's good!

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:51.030
This is Yuuichi-san's soccer?

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.730
He's overwhelming them!

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.490
Tenma-kun, your Avatar!

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:58.610
Let's go!

00:08:58.610 --> 00:08:59.040
Okay!

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:06.420
Demon Soldier Pendragon!

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:12.860
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:48.490
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:50.680
Armed!

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:58.060
Yuuichi-san can use Avatar Armed too?!

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.230
Tenma!

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:01.390
You can do it too! Try it!

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:04.180
I can do it too...

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:05.880
Let's do this!

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:08.340
Demon God Pegasus Arc!

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:17.620
Armed!

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.280
You were right!

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:33.660
I did it!

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.460
I can use Avatar Armed too!

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:39.180
Now, let's go!

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:39.560
Okay!

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:46.890
Ruler of the Skies, Phoenix!

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:52.010
Armed!

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.830
Alpha goes Avatar Armed too!

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:14.460
Keeper Command 03!

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.140
<Boom Shout>

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:24.960
Goal!

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.070
Tenmas win their second point!

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:33.070
You did great.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:34.780
Thank you.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:37.020
What a powerful helper.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:41.940
This is hot! And it's getting hotter!!

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.160
Pathetic, Alpha.

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:48.080
Chairman...

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:50.740
Yes.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:53.120
We are retreating.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.010
W-What's that?

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.930
A UFO?

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:10.400
We protected the founding of Endou Mamoru's soccer club...

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:12.270
We protected it!

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.760
So that means... we won, right?

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:15.110
Yes!

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:16.810
I have no idea what's going on here...

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:18.980
Thank you, Yuuichi-san!

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:21.600
Let me help you in your fight.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.280
You?

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:25.550
For Kyousuke.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:30.840
Tenma-kun.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:33.100
From what you know about my past,

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:40.190
I lost my ability to play soccer in an accident that occurred when I was twelve and Kyousuke was seven.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:41.780
Right?

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:43.730
Yes.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:46.460
Well, that accident didn't happen.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:50.170
As a result, both Kyousuke and I were able to continue soccer.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:55.660
We grew to such a level that we were offered the chance to study soccer abroad.

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:57.800
Study abroad? Wow!

00:12:58.530 --> 00:12:59.640
But...

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:02.450
Can't we do something?

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:06.020
Being able to study soccer abroad would be such a wonderful opportunity for them.

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:09.590
It's unfortunate, but we're not affluent enough to send them both.

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:11.220
The most we can do is send one.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.460
Oh, no...

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.350
If there was only some way...

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.570
I want to send the both of them too, if it was possible.

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:20.980
They both may turn out to be incredible players in the future.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.530
I'm not going.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:31.370
Yuuichi!

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:33.160
Let Kyousuke go instead.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.180
You were listening?

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:36.190
You go, Nii-san.

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:41.110
I'm fed up with soccer anyway.

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:44.000
Kyousuke...

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.280
Tsurugi did that?

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.250
There's no way he meant what he said.

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:53.340
But Kyousuke got rid of everything he owned that had to do with soccer.

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:56.040
He even stopped kicking the ball completely.

00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:00.020
It was Kyousuke's way of showing the greatest extent of his kindness.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:04.560
That's why I chose to study abroad for his sake.

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:11.430
It was a set-up by El Dorado to steal soccer from Tsurugi Kyousuke, wasn't it?

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:14.140
And it would have worked...

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:19.410
But then they showed up in front of me to try and steal soccer from me.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:20.900
They attacked you, too?

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:28.130
You must have greatly influenced a multitude of soccer youths in your new timeline.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:29.910
That's why they targeted you.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:36.480
But the reason why I'm able to play soccer now and travel through time to get here...

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.160
...is because someone helped me.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:45.410
That person didn't say their name, but they told me they supported people like us who loved soccer.

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:47.310
Support people like us...

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:48.440
Who love soccer...

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:54.720
Not only did that person save me, but they gave me this Time Bracelet.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:57.480
With this, I can travel through time.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:02.450
I still don't get much of it, but this is a fight to protect soccer, right?

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:03.510
Yes.

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:05.650
Then I want to join you guys!

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:09.540
Endou-kun, your priority right now is to make the soccer club.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:12.410
That would be your way of protecting soccer, won't it?

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.840
Yes, she's right!

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:17.250
If you make the soccer club, soccer would be so happy!

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.200
You're a funny guy.

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:22.420
Now, gentlemen!

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:25.960
Let us hold this elation within our hearts and return to our previous timeline!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:27.560
Okay!

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:29.640
We're time jumping, huh?

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:31.180
You're leaving already?

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:37.600
Since we've averted the crisis in Endou-kun's timeline, we need to check how it's affected ours.

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:39.080
For Yuuichi-san too.

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:45.710
Tenma.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:46.790
Yes?

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:50.550
I'll get the Raimon soccer club off the ground no matter what.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.120
It's a promise!

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:54.580
And I'll do my best to keep soccer safe!

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.750
Yeah! So if we meet again...

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.940
Let's play soccer!

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:05.620
In 5 seconds!

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:06.460
4...

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:07.380
3...

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:08.440
2...

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.410
1...

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:10.820
Time jump!

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.660
I feel like I'm still dreaming.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:17.610
I'm sure I'll meet Tenma again.

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.090
I just get that feeling.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:25.720
The doorplate!

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:32.430
When history changes and it becomes inconvenient for the Artifact to be here, it returns to where it originally belongs.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:35.240
Back to Coach Endou's time, right?

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:36.110
Now you're getting it.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:40.550
Coach Endou mastered God Hand even though he was only a first-year.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:41.840
Will history be okay?

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:43.630
Don't worry.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:49.470
The changes in space-time that are brought about by parallel worlds are a lot more mysterious and interesting than you think.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:53.640
Well, sure, they may be more interesting, but they also make everything a little more complicated.

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:56.610
In any case, this was a pretty tiring day.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:58.810
Tenma, let's go to your house.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:04.950
Guests?

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:06.110
Good evening.

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:09.800
Aki-nee, they're all sleeping over in my room today.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.310
Sasuke, that's okay with you, right?

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:14.980
This puppy is the one from back then?

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:17.280
Yeah, he's called Sasuke.

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.530
Nice to meet you, Sasuke.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.830
I'm sorry for the sudden intrusion. We're much obliged to you.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:25.020
Oh, you don't have to worry about feeding me.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.810
Huh? Have I seen you somewhere before?

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:30.320
Alpha.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:34.570
That was quite a poor turn of developments for Protocol Omega.

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:37.190
Do you have something to say for yourself?

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:38.030
No, sir.

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:40.220
Incompetence is a sin.

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.360
If you disgrace yourself one more time...

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:44.520
Understood?

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.490
Yes, master.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:52.530
What's wrong?

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:54.340
Let's go inside.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:57.780
But what if there are different clubs in there again?

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:03.330
Then I'll call Wondeba over so we can time jump and fix it.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:05.730
Was it a good idea to have left him behind, to begin with?

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:09.090
In this timeline, he'll only scare everyone off.

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:14.010
He's washing the caravan...

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:15.960
Huh? Tenma?

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:16.740
Aoi!

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.720
Practice is starting soon.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.860
Practice... for the calligraphy club?

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:23.720
What are you talking about?

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:25.160
The soccer club!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:25.940
The soccer club!

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.120
It's back to normal!

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:31.220
Tenma, who are these people?

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.650
Um, uh...

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:34.330
I'm Fei.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.300
One of Tenma's soccer pals.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:38.630
We're here to take a look at Raimon's soccer club today.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:41.090
Tenma's friends, huh?

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.740
Everyone, we have guests today!

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.610
Tenma, you're late!

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:48.500
I thought you wouldn't be coming today!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.420
Thank goodness!

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:51.940
What's wrong?

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:53.900
Hello!

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:54.910
Hello.

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:56.920
Tsurugi-senpai!

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:58.860
It's been awhile, Tsurugi-senpai!

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:01.890
Is he a Raimon alumni?

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:04.200
Oh right, you first-years wouldn't know who he is.

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:09.360
Tsurugi-senpai has pulled the team along as Raimon's ace striker.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.170
Even now when he's graduated, he still visits-

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:12.390
Wait! Then what about Tsurugi?

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.040
He's right there, don't speak of him so disrespectfully!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:17.260
No, I mean Tsurugi Kyousuke!

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:18.370
Yuuichi-san's younger brother!

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:21.340
Things aren't fully back to normal yet?

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:24.020
Let's get everyone involved for this one.

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:25.080
How?

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:45.230
Good grief, I was in the middle of washing the caravan, you know!

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:47.530
It talked!

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:48.770
What is that thing?

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:50.610
How rude!

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:54.730
I'm the coach of Tenmas, Clark Wonderbat-sama!

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:57.270
A bear?

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:58.410
Who are you calling a bear?!

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:00.170
Tenma, what is going on here?

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:02.450
Let me explain.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:07.710
And that's that.

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:11.120
Did you get all of that, everyone?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.740
I know this talk about time jumping has all of your heads spinning...

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:18.630
but as you've just heard, this life I'm living right now is a lie.

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:21.590
The "me" that he knows is the real me.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:27.870
That's why I want to take back the real me and give soccer back to Kyousuke.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:34.050
It also means that you as Raimon's soccer club will return to being the soccer club you are meant to be.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:38.900
So we're all living a life of lies...

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:40.530
Yes.

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:44.960
You make it sound like I'm not myself. That doesn't give me a good feeling.

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:47.260
This is no good for me, I'm lost.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:47.990
So am I.

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:50.320
All of this just flew over my head.

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:51.700
Why are you looking so proud about it?

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.430
I get it.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:56.650
I'm a big science fiction fan.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:21:00.030
Knowing that there are other versions of me in parallel worlds is like a dream come true!

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:01.440
You aren't ordinary.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:02.840
Um...

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:08.090
The real Yuuichi-san lost the ability to play soccer because of an injury, right?

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:08.720
Yeah.

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:15.290
Since time has already changed and all, can't we keep it so the both of you get to play soccer in this new timeline?

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.430
Yeah, that's the best way.

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:20.910
Right! It's a chance you should take.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:22.020
Thank you.

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:27.240
But I don't think we're allowed to do that without severe consequences.

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:29.870
I want to bring soccer back to Kyousuke.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:33.490
He loves soccer even more than I do.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:39.310
Saving Kyousuke will save Raimon's soccer club.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:42.020
Please help me, everyone.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:42.770
Okay!

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:47.160
Tsurugi...

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.940
What are you doing right now?

00:23:23.950 --> 00:23:25.620
Tsurugi and Yuuichi-san.

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:27.870
Soccer guides both of their fates.

00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:30.710
Now both of their wishes combine!

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:33.280
Next, The Last Soccer.

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:35.200
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:48.840
The Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone's proverb today is...

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:55.750
The ball isn't meant to hurt people!

00:23:55.750 --> 00:23:56.620
That's all!
